  "Question": "Which points need to be listed, at a minimum, to draw the graph of $y=2x-1$?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "$(0,1)$ and $(1,-1)$",
    "B": "Only the single point $(0,-1)$ is needed.",
    "C": "$(0,-1)$ and $(1,1)$",
    "D": "$(0,0)$ and $(1,1)$"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The graph of a linear function is a straight line, and two points determine a straight line. When $x=0$, $y=-1$; when $x=1$, $y=1$. Therefore, use $(0,-1)$ and $(1,1)$.",
